WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.867
A Common Table Expression begins with WITH.

00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:07.602
Think of it as a named intermediate relation inside one statement.

00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:11.222
The first stage can summarize or clean the source.

00:00:11.222 --> 00:00:14.497
A later stage can join or enrich that result.

00:00:14.497 --> 00:00:17.712
The final SELECT consumes the prepared data.

00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:22.772
Naming the stages helps you reason about the transformation one step at a time.

00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:28.992
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:28.992 --> 00:00:36.462
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a

00:00:36.462 --> 00:00:43.600
new block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
